// The out value `array:` names is an `Array`, or an `Option` of one; and `@c` on a field belongs to
// a struct mirror.
// error: out value 1 of the C binding `notArray`, `glyphs`, is `Glyph` in Avin and `as_glyph *` in C: the array C answers is copied into an `Array`, or an `Option` of one for null
// error: `@c` on a field names the C field a field of a C struct mirror mirrors, and `Plain` mirrors no C struct

@c(struct: "as_glyph")
data Glyph(index: long, x: real, y: real)

data Plain(@c("x") x: int)

@c("void as_glyphs(out as_glyph **glyphs, out int *count)", array: "glyphs", length: "count")
notArray() -> (Glyph, int)

main() = 0
